@@ -25,3 +25,48 @@ storage is `bun:sqlite`, and the HTTP layer is `Bun.serve`.
 response shapes, status codes, and pagination. Every validation failure,
 on every endpoint, returns the same fixed error shape documented there as
 `#/components/schemas/Error`.
+
+## Running locally
+
+```sh
+bun install
+DATABASE_PATH=./inventory.sqlite bun run migrate
+DATABASE_PATH=./inventory.sqlite PORT=4175 bun run start
+```
+
+Both environment variables are required by the server. Startup also runs the
+idempotent schema migration before opening the listening socket. The database's
+parent directory must already exist. `GET /health` returns `{"status":"ok"}`.
+
+```sh
+bun run test
+bun run typecheck
+```
+
+Tests cover the HTTP contract, malformed requests, pagination, concurrent stock
+updates, repeated migrations, and persistence through a server restart. Temporary
+test databases stay inside the ignored `.test-data/` directory and are cleaned up.
+
+## Storage and stock behavior
+
+The schema lives in `migrations/001_inventory.sql`. Products and warehouses have
+unique SKU/code constraints; movements reference both and have a unique
+idempotency key. All request values are passed as SQL parameters.
+
+Stock is the sum of movements across all warehouses: receipts add quantity,
+shipments subtract it, and adjustments apply a signed delta. Negative product
+totals are rejected. Low-stock results use a strict `stock < reorderThreshold`
+comparison and include products with no movements when their threshold is positive.
+
+An immediate SQLite transaction handles replay detection, the stock check, and
+movement insertion together. Replays compare all body fields regardless of JSON
+property order and return the original movement, including its original
+`resultingStock`. An omitted note differs from an empty note. Rejected movements
+do not consume their idempotency key. WAL mode and a busy timeout coordinate
+connections sharing the same database file.
+
+Lists have stable creation-time/ID ordering, default to page 1 with 20 rows, and
+allow at most 100 rows per page. Request integers must be exactly representable
+as JavaScript safe integers; stock changes that would exceed that range are
+rejected. Unknown body properties, unsupported query parameters, and duplicate
+pagination parameters return the contract's validation error envelope.
